<details class='sub-section' id='sub_1'><summary class='sub-header'><span><span class='arrow-icon'>▶</span>02 · 恋爱、吸引、分手与决裂 <span style='font-weight:400;font-size:0.86em;color:#cbd5e1;margin-left:8px;'>Falling for, Breaking up & Falling out</span></span><span class='sub-meta'>25 义项</span></summary><div class='epe-explain-box'>🎭 <b>场景认知导读：</b>两人绑定成一个整体后碎裂即分手（break/split up），从原本共同所属的友谊圈子里掉出去即反目成仇（fall out）。</div><table><tr><th width='21%'>Phrasal Verb • 语法与语域</th><th width='24%'>🎯 English Definition (WordNet)</th><th width='14%'>🔄 Single-Word Verb</th><th width='41%'>💬 Authentic Examples</th></tr>
<tr data-sep='Inseparable' data-reg='Informal'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>ask <span class='pt-highlight'>for</span></span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Inseparable'>🔵 不可拆分 (v. + prep. + O)</span><span class='reg-Informal' title='🤖 自动判定依据：语料库日常/小说会话分布活跃 + 作为正式词 [invite] 的日常短语替身' style='cursor:help;'>💬 口语/日常 (Informal)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>increase the likelihood of</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>invite, arouse</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>①</span><b>Ask</b> <b>for</b> trouble.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>②</span>Invite criticism.</div></div></div></td></tr>
